        "notes": "## \ud83d\udd25 **POWERSPIKE** \ud83d\udd25\n\n---\n\n# \ud83e\uddff Items\n\nNow you should be around ~20k money. We will pivot on AP.\n\nTake  [Clone Conjuration](item_6c9f6be1-ab29-4f46-af24-34e4835f9af3) or  [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b) depending on what power you started.\n\nTake  [Donut Delivery](item_296adb69-d517-4885-903a-ef8f3a1d6a7b) and  [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) in priority. Why? Because the more you spam your TP and suzu, the more you'll heal and guess what... you'll get more money. It's always about money (like IRL?).\n\nIf you need survival, think about buying  [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0).\n\n# \ud83d\udd2b Playstyle\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you have a Queen, DVA or Zarya you can stick with your tank because they'll most likely try to push into the enemy backline. Use your TP on cooldown, it's a big burst of healing and your clone will participate.\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f Use your Suzu not only as a cleanse tool, but as a **healing tool**. ATM of the game, you'll get enough AP to give ~20% life of your tank with one Suzu. So you can often use it because of  [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b). But watch for your cooldown, mostly if there is a Queen/DVA/Junk ult coming.",
